; Duke Dungeon — a map drawn once: a dungeon that has stopped changing.
;
; The castle kits' proof (art/castles/export_castles.py): a little courtyard built of
; FelikinRuslan's rampart pieces (CC BY 4.0) -- towers on grid points five cells apart,
; a wall of three cells between each two, placed at the cell after a tower and turned
; by its facing (0 east, 90 north, 180 west, 270 south) -- the gate in the south wall,
; the queen's dark keep inside (the fort's keep drawn with its dark picture), a basin, a
; table, a barrel and a crate from the castle room. Not a level: a page for the eye, with one
; skeleton to win it. Its walls stand in the way; its gate lets the hero in.

